topped the first rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56699, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01W3EFikHhShD8UAqLsnAPgu", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56699, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01W3EFikHhShD8UAqLsnAPgu", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59157, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SGWoePC54vazjhVzMEzTgF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59457, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SGWoePC54vazjhVzMEzTgF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59457, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SGWoePC54vazjhVzMEzTgF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64878, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create it timed out, but INC-0001 had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. That means on-call was paged once, not twice. The incident describes what happened and the rollback, and lists two follow-ups:\n  1. Find out why v2.3.1 is failing health checks before deploying it again.\n  2. Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QkpV8U3msuGTi476dQ1Hpq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013tcf18EAaKw8EcnQ7BypVt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1; seq 2 and 3 are both unhealthy). Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WfFPwUiDcnfBfcdtzCSQJ9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BT95gViz1CuFnKH4TfYGof", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through, so I'm retrying it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0181h14HtEV9qMqHnLuxK5pn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BpHcdoGmyZh7XBsSGxn2MS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XZct4KRpNcPMYhZxheU8Xz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01W3EFikHhShD8UAqLsnAPgu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed. Before the rollback it was unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The two releases before it (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1) were both unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release and was chosen as the rollback target. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt succeeded, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. After the rollback the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-ups: (1) find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures before redeploying; (2) investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before retrying. A second one would page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SGWoePC54vazjhVzMEzTgF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create it timed out, but INC-0001 had been created anyway, so I didn't retry. That means on-call was paged once, not twice. The incident describes what happened and the rollback, and lists two follow-ups:\n  1. Find out why v2.3.1 is failing health checks before deploying it again.\n  2. Investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}